6. |Case|:**manage_books**
**Pseudocode from Project 2:**
```
FUNCTION books() [GET/POST]  
    IF session['username'] NOT EXISTS  
        REDIRECT /login  
    IF POST REQUEST  
        title = FORM_DATA['title']  
        author = FORM_DATA['author']  
        isbn = FORM_DATA['isbn']  
        BookManager.add_book(title, author, isbn)  
    book_list = BookManager.list_books()  
    RENDER books.html WITH books=book_list  
END  

FUNCTION add_book(title, author, isbn)  
    APPEND (title, author, isbn) TO books.txt  
    RETURN True (or False on failure)  
END  

FUNCTION delete_book(isbn)  
    READ books.txt  
    FILTER OUT book WHERE book[2] == isbn  
    WRITE remaining books back to file  
    RETURN True (or False on failure)  
END  
```
**Key Libraries:**  
- **Flask (url_for, redirect)**: Handles URL routing and redirection.

**Pseudocode from Project 3:**
```
ROUTE /books  
    IF user NOT in session  
        REDIRECT to login  
    ELSE  
        IF POST request  
            IF delete_isbn provided  
                CALL library.delete_book(isbn)  
                    READ books.txt  
                    REMOVE book with matching ISBN  
                    WRITE remaining books back  
            ELSE  
                CALL library.add_book(title, author, isbn)  
                    APPEND book to books.txt  
        RENDER books.html  
            FORM for adding books (title, author, ISBN)  
            TABLE listing all books with delete buttons  
```
**Key Functionality:**  
- CRUD operations on books via file I/O (`books.txt`).  
- Uses Flask `request.form` to handle POST data.

